description:
Provide persistent conversation history to the normal `AgentRuntime.run`, `start`, and `stream` entry points through an Effect Layer:

```ts
const HistoryLive = PersistentHistory.layer.pipe(
  Layer.provide(sqliteStore({ filename: "./history.sqlite" })),
);

const program = Effect.gen(function* () {
  yield* AgentRuntime.run(agent, firstInput, { conversationId });
  yield* AgentRuntime.run(agent, secondInput, { conversationId });
  const history = yield* ConversationHistory;
  return yield* history.load(conversationId);
}).pipe(Effect.provide(HistoryLive), Effect.scoped);
```

`ConversationHistory` is an explicit runtime requirement. Provide `ConversationHistory.layerTransient` for existing execution without retained history. The engine owns the lifecycle; `PersistentHistory.layer` captures the store and stages each Run independently. Spawned children inherit their parent's history policy. The durable coordinator supplies transient policy internally because its existing journal owns recovery and canonical commits.

A successful Run appends its encoded input, exact native Prompt suffix, and completion in one batch. Model resources close before commit. Result decoding for `run` and `start.await` also precedes commit, and observers see `RunCompleted` only after persistence succeeds. Schema transformations are not repeated to create history. Failed or interrupted execution before commit leaves prior history intact; storage failure after commit can leave the entire Run recorded. External effects are never automatically retried.

Writers use epoch zero and compare the loaded tail. Conflicts, fencing, incompatible durable history, and persistence bounds become typed `ConversationHistoryError` reasons. The 65,536-record export limit is checked before external execution. Canonical store and durable append behavior remain unchanged.

Checkpoint storage becomes an optional capability:

```ts
// Before
yield* store.saveCheckpoint(request);

// After
if (store.checkpoints !== undefined) {
  yield* store.checkpoints.save(request);
}
```

Memory, SQLite, Cloudflare, and routing retain checkpoint support for explicit consumers such as the published Travel Planner fixture. The base conformance suite no longer requires it, and administrative verification skips checkpoint checks when unsupported. `UserInputRecorded.submissionId` is optional for immediate history.

Validation: `vp run ready`; 19 history regressions covering restart, all execution entry points, native messages, Schema boundaries, resource closure, concurrent writers, fencing, conflicting history ownership, failure/interruption, append failpoints, and the export limit. The offline SQLite example also saved and loaded history across separate processes.

Closes [KOM-8](https://linear.app/reve-ai/issue/KOM-8).

Completed `AgentRuntime.run` calls unnecessarily required a caller `Scope`, even though the stream consumer already finishes run-owned work and finalizers before returning. Remove that extra requirement so a fully provided, self-contained Run can execute directly:

```ts
// Before
AgentRuntime.run(agent, input).pipe(Effect.provide(AppLive), Effect.scoped);

// After
AgentRuntime.run(agent, input).pipe(Effect.provide(AppLive));
```

Caller-contributed `Scope` and other dependencies remain visible. The existing cleanup → result validation → history commit → observable completion ordering stays intact. `start` keeps its caller-owned execution and replay lifetime, and shared application Layers retain their composition lifetime. Wrapping public `run` in `Effect.scoped` or excluding `Scope` from all requirements would erase genuine caller dependencies.

Type proofs cover all three entry points and scoped instructions, input projection, hooks, and output decoding. Lifecycle regressions check cleanup before return or fiber completion and observer termination when a detached owner closes. Update the guides and SQLite consumer, add the engine patch changeset, and regenerate both Action bundles.

Validation: `vp run ready` and the offline SQLite `history seed` / `history show` smoke check across separate processes.

Closes [KOM-12](https://linear.app/reve-ai/issue/KOM-12).
